Stochastic modeling can help you make predictions about outcomes when random factors are involved. It includes uncertainty and, because of this, gives you a range of possibilities and probabilities. Stochastic modeling is commonly used in the finance and insurance industries to make investment and risk management decisions. It is also applied in life sciences and engineering. It's also suitable in fields like weather forecasting because of how complex, unpredictable, and random weather systems are. is relevant
